## 1. 7 Main Phases of STLC

| STLC Phase                    | What happens for a Login feature                                                                           |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1. Requirement Analysis**   | The tester studies requirements such as valid login, wrong password, forgot password, and account lockout. |
| **2. Test Planning**          | The testing team decides the testing approach, resources, tools, and time required for Login testing.      |
| **3. Test Case Design**       | Test cases are prepared for valid credentials, invalid credentials, blank fields, password rules, etc.     |
| **4. Test Environment Setup** | A suitable mobile/web environment, database, browser, and test accounts are prepared.                      |
| **5. Test Execution**         | Testers run the Login test cases and compare the actual results with expected results.                     |
| **6. Defect Reporting**       | Any problems found during testing are reported to developers with proper details and evidence.             |
| **7. Test Closure**           | Testing is completed, results are summarized, and lessons learned are recorded for future testing.         |

---

## 2. Entry and Exit Criteria for Each STLC Phase

| STLC Phase         | Entry Criteria                                              | Exit Criteria                                                          |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Planning**       | Login requirements are available and understood.            | Test strategy, resources, and schedule are finalized.                  |
| **Monitoring**     | Testing activities have started.                            | Progress, defects, and test coverage are regularly tracked.            |
| **Analysis**       | Requirements and acceptance criteria are available.         | Testable requirements and testing conditions are identified.           |
| **Design**         | Test conditions are identified.                             | Test cases, test data, and expected results are prepared and reviewed. |
| **Implementation** | Approved test cases are available.                          | Test environment and required test data are ready for execution.       |
| **Execution**      | Build is available and test environment is working.         | Planned test cases are executed and results are recorded.              |
| **Reporting**      | Test execution results and defect details are available.    | Test results and major defects are communicated to the team.           |
| **Closure**        | Testing objectives are completed and results are available. | Final report is prepared and testing is officially closed.             |

